wlan: keep the start-window diagnostics behind t1100_readback

The stock driver, right after the firmware sections are downloaded, goes
straight to wlanConfigWifiFunc(FALSE, 0) and then polls WCIR for
WCIR_WLAN_READY.  Our port still issued two unconditional diagnostics in
that window: an INIT_CMD_ID_QUERY_PENDING_ERROR (wlanImageQueryStatus)
and the t1100_hif_state("after-download") register dump, which reads
WCIR/WASR/D2HRM0R/CPUPCR/WHLPCR plus the raw HIF window and SPM state.

Both now live under t1100_readback, so a run with t1100_readback=0 keeps
the start window byte-for-byte as quiet as the vendor path.

Signed-off-by: T1100 port <t1100@localhost>
---
--- a/common/wlan_lib.c
+++ b/common/wlan_lib.c
@@ -1314,13 +1314,13 @@
 		 * just received (INIT_CMD_ID_QUERY_PENDING_ERROR). With
 		 * CFG_ENABLE_FW_DOWNLOAD_ACK=1 the normal path never does this.
 		 */
-		{
+		if (t1100_readback) {
 			WLAN_STATUS u4QueryStatus = wlanImageQueryStatus(prAdapter);
 
 			pr_info("t1100-query: wlanImageQueryStatus() -> %u (0=ok)\n",
 				(UINT_32)u4QueryStatus);
+			t1100_hif_state(prAdapter, "after-download");
 		}
-		t1100_hif_state(prAdapter, "after-download");
 
 		/*
 		 * T1100 M22: hand the ROMv4 patch to the MCU ROM before asking it
